{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/472801-help-i-love-vtr2-and-my-players-love-vtm","id":472801,"title":"Help! I love VtR2 and my players love VtM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-08T08:31:13-07:00","id":472801,"title":"Help! I love VtR2 and my players love VtM","content":"We all agree that we love the clans of VtM, but there's a huge gap in our love for cWoD. What do we do? I'd rather just use VtR2 with the Translation Guide.<br /> <br /> 1. I really like Blood Potency (I really love Spirit from <a href=\"http://vampirerpg.free.fr/Rules/Anne-Rice.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://vampirerpg.free.fr/Rules/Anne-Rice.html</a>) as opposed to the uber-stat that is Generation;<br /> 2. I love the mystery and myth of no-single-creation myth of VtR2 as opposed to &quot;we all come from Caine, and he really exists);<br /> 3. I love the tuned WW v2 post-God-Machine mechanics;<br /> 4. I love the weirdness of monsters and other splats (heck there are whole books of make your own creatures with bizarre dread powers);<br /> 5. I love the new rules for Humanity and touchstones, particularly with banes hacked in. Really intensely dislike alternate paths of humanity, etc.;<br /> 6. I love the no-metaplot, world not populated with figures who are way more canonically important than you.<br /> <br /> What do we do? If I've discovered one thing about myself as a GM is that I have to be REALLY INTO what I'm doing/running to be an effective GM? I CAN'T be the first GM who has run into this problem!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3927-demon15","name":"Demon15","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:20:03-07:00","id":472902,"title":"","content":"My first question would be what do the players love specifically about VtM? You told us what you like about VtR, but not what draws them to Masquerade. Once we know what they like besides the Clans, we might be able to find a compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:23:36-07:00","id":472910,"title":"","content":"I won't guess! I'll just ask them. Give me a sec.!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3927-demon15","name":"Demon15","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:37:20-07:00","id":472920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/472801-help-i-love-vtr2-and-my-players-love-vtm#post472801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We all agree that we love the clans of VtM, but there's a huge gap in our love for cWoD. What do we do? I'd rather just use VtR2 with the Translation Guide.<br /> <br /> 1. I really like Blood Potency (I really love Spirit from <a href=\"http://vampirerpg.free.fr/Rules/Anne-Rice.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://vampirerpg.free.fr/Rules/Anne-Rice.html</a>) as opposed to the uber-stat that is Generation;<br /> 2. I love the mystery and myth of no-single-creation myth of VtR2 as opposed to &quot;we all come from Caine, and he really exists);<br /> 3. I love the tuned WW v2 post-God-Machine mechanics;<br /> 4. I love the weirdness of monsters and other splats (heck there are whole books of make your own creatures with bizarre dread powers);<br /> 5. I love the new rules for Humanity and touchstones, particularly with banes hacked in. Really intensely dislike alternate paths of humanity, etc.;<br /> 6. I love the no-metaplot, world not populated with figures who are way more canonically important than you.<br /> <br /> What do we do? If I've discovered one thing about myself as a GM is that I have to be REALLY INTO what I'm doing/running to be an effective GM? I CAN'T be the first GM who has run into this problem!</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, I highly suggest using <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\">Yossarian's 13 Licks update to the Vampire Translation Guide</a>, the guide is optional when using 13 licks but not required. Use this to run a 'Masquiem' setting, as I plan to once I've sorted out a character sheet with Mask, Dirge, Generation, and the term Blood Pool instead of Vitae (personal preference), as well as a version with Blood Potency instead of Generation.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to point out that Blood Potency is more of an uber-stat than generation (it is rolled to resist ANYTHING supernatural), it's just priced accordingly, unlike generation. If using Masquerade I'd suggest increasing the cost of Generation to 2-3 background points, and possibly getting rid of the immunity to dominate that it gives (as I do, it makes it far more difficult to determine somebody's generation). I'd say make it 1 point for levels 1-3 (one blood point isn't that big of a deal), and 2 points for levels 4 and 5 (levels 6+ aren't available to PCs), without the immunity to dominate that it normally grants, although really I suggest using Requiem and either having Blood Potency or just treating Generation as being equal to 14-Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> Remember that you don't have to use any clans that you don't want to, I like to swap out the Settites for the Mekhet (with their 'role' being priests and mystics), and that how much history is known is up to you (my vampires know that vampires existed in the times of Ancient Rome, when the Camarilla was active, but not since then), along with any rules (I'm not fond of paths either).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:02:25-07:00","id":473302,"title":"","content":"There are ways of porting things over depending on what they like or don't like.<br /> You might try V20 as well as I hear it is metaplot agnostic.<br /> Feel free to PM me if you need suggestions but first you need to know what they like about Masq.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:50:18-07:00","id":473375,"title":"","content":"Foot-dragging I've experienced in the past, and some shoe-horned ideas for address:<br /> <br /> <b>Only five clans?</b><br /> <br /> Let players start out as bloodlines right off the bat. A lot of the bloodlines will have some thematic elements that a player can hook onto, and many of the old Clans make pseudo- or direct appearances (Lasombra / Khaibit; Malkavians / Malkovians; Torador / Toreador; Giovanni / Sangiovanni). Lots of people hated that there were no Tremere. I always point them to the Ordo. Big gap I can remember is no Tzmisce equivalent. And yes - there are bloodline and full clan conversions out there as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenants are weird.</b><br /> <br /> If they really like the old structure of Cam / Anarch / Sabbat, those do still play out in reflections within the Covenants. Cam = Invictus, Anarchs = Carthians, Sabbat = Crone and/or Theban, and it shouldn't be difficult to play up those rivalries.<br /> <br /> <b>My Clan's Discipline spread was nerfed.</b><br /> <br /> While I really enjoy the focusing on the five archetypes for Requiem Clans, I remember a lot of people were apprehensive during the shift. (Ventrue lose Presence and get Animalism? <i>Lame!</i>) Especially in Blood and Smoke, this is mitigated by the disciplines being a lot more powerful or a lot more story driven (usually both). Also, you can mitigate this by hand-waving out-of-clans. Just let people buy whatever basic disciplines they want without worrying about teachers, etc (if they have the XP). You could even just middle the XP cost - all discplines are Level*4XP (or 4 Experiences) to raise giving everyone a chance to spread out wherever.<br /> <br /> <b>Where did Generation go?</b><br /> <br /> The switch from Gen to BP was one of my favorite mechanical changes. While in my games I ditch the merits-for-BP discount, players who really like to go low-gen can start at BP 3 if they ditch some starting merit dots. Also, you can just start people at 2 BP (allowing for Bloodlines) with a hand-wave. For people that liked the thematic element of Elders / Ancillae / Neonates based on the Generational scale, take a look at the Invictus Dynasties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T16:01:49-07:00","id":473471,"title":"","content":"Assuming OP is my friend whose name starts with a G (since they bugged me to post): I like the masquerade clans, their thematic elements, and their inter clan interactions better as a whole.<br /> <br /> I also never had a great deal of love for modern (default) masquerade: dark ages is where it's at for me. <br /> <br /> Decide to run it v20? Restrict generation to 1 to 3. Decide to run it Requiem? I've read the translation guide and the mechanical changes don't bother me at all (though I'd prefer the masquerade clans outright replaced the Requiem clans in such a scenario, and that the &quot;as a Requiem bloodline&quot; sections were ignored). <br /> <br /> In either case dark ages is an ideal setting from masquerade to do basically any changes you want, since the only antedeluvian related plot at that point is saulot/Tremere (which can fairly easily just be the Tremere's propaganda to give legitimacy to a made up clan of mortals that ritualistically became vampires). Caine is in the traditions and myth, sure, but does he exist? Really doesn't matter; it's religion. Do the antediluvians exist? Doesn't really matter. On top of PCs never meeting any (unless it's that type of game) the idea of the jyhad being real is the threat. It doesn't matter if someone is pulling the strings so long as the threat of someone invisibly manipulating you is there.<br /> <br /> For me, I just want to make my dark ages lasombra and I don't much care how that happens mechanically; the character (the idea) will translate in either system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5603-faaln","name":"Faaln","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T17:06:32-07:00","id":473522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faaln</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/472801-help-i-love-vtr2-and-my-players-love-vtm?p=473471#post473471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming OP is my friend whose name starts with a G (since they bugged me to post): I like the masquerade clans, their thematic elements, and their inter clan interactions better as a whole.<br /> <br /> I also never had a great deal of love for modern (default) masquerade: dark ages is where it's at for me.<br /> <br /> Decide to run it v20? Restrict generation to 1 to 3. Decide to run it Requiem? I've read the translation guide and the mechanical changes don't bother me at all (though I'd prefer the masquerade clans outright replaced the Requiem clans in such a scenario, and that the &quot;as a Requiem bloodline&quot; sections were ignored).<br /> <br /> In either case dark ages is an ideal setting from masquerade to do basically any changes you want, since the only antedeluvian related plot at that point is saulot/Tremere (which can fairly easily just be the Tremere's propaganda to give legitimacy to a made up clan of mortals that ritualistically became vampires). Caine is in the traditions and myth, sure, but does he exist? Really doesn't matter; it's religion. Do the antediluvians exist? Doesn't really matter. On top of PCs never meeting any (unless it's that type of game) the idea of the jyhad being real is the threat. It doesn't matter if someone is pulling the strings so long as the threat of someone invisibly manipulating you is there.<br /> <br /> For me, I just want to make my dark ages lasombra and I don't much care how that happens mechanically; the character (the idea) will translate in either system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soooo, your saying you like the clans (Without any concrete details other than 'interactions'?) You realize there are complex interactions among Requiem's covenants in much the same way, Requiem can be played in &quot;Dark Ages' and even has a few excellent historical books for working with those (Even though they are 1e). Basically most of what your after is still there, but the clan vs clan dynamics are more Covenant vs Covenant (Your character gets to pick those).<br /> <br /> I get the feeling your not especially familiar with 2e Requiem or the full requiem line. Have you read the Clan Books or Covenant Books? What about Danse Macabre? You might surprise yourself if you looked into those as to how your perceptions change. I came initially from Masquerade, so I understand the perceptions coming from one to the other, but I've grown to love requiem, especially with the advent of 2e.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:58:55-07:00","id":475077,"title":"","content":"You could tweak the khaibit for a Losombra<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Shadow and the Asp &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T05:05:02-07:00","id":475639,"title":"","content":"Let someone mention the <b>Vampire Translation Guide</b>. Use it as a compromise at the least - your players get to play in their preferred setting but you get to add in mysterious creatures in the corners all while using your preferred rules set","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T00:19:18-07:00","id":476736,"title":"","content":"Considering what the OP seems to like in B&amp;S when compared to what Faaln seems to like about VtM I'd say you should perhaps read through <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\">Yossarians 13 Licks</a>, as suggested by someone above, as that allows you to port VtM Clans into B&amp;S mechanics allowing you to keep VtM fluff and still using the new mechanics if that is what Demon15 prefers and Faaln is too picky about a system as long as he gets his character. It shouldn't be any problem at all using the 13 Licks in VtM's Dark Ages setting either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}